# Motorline Auto

Motorline Auto is an ASP.NET Core MVC dealership app for two Pennsylvania locations, Altoona and State College. It uses .NET 10, Entity Framework Core, SQLite, and ASP.NET Core Identity.

- Customers can browse inventory, filter by vehicle type, make, year, price, and dealership, and open listings to see specifications and photos.
- Customers can estimate monthly payments using a down payment, credit score, and loan term.
- Managers can add and edit listings, upload vehicle photos, assign dealership locations, and review sold, pending or reserved, and total inventory counts.

## Seed the vehicle catalog

From the folder containing car-dealership.csproj, run this command to import model years 1996–2027 for a selection of common U.S.-market makes. The importer applies database migrations and needs internet access to reach the NHTSA vehicle catalog.

```powershell
dotnet run -p:UseAppHost=false -- --import-catalog --from 1996 --to 2027 --makes "Toyota,Honda,Ford,Chevrolet,Nissan,Hyundai,Kia,Subaru,Jeep,Ram,GMC,Dodge,Volkswagen,Mazda,BMW,Mercedes-Benz,Lexus,Tesla,Mitsubishi,Buick"
```

This fills the make, model, and year options used when adding a vehicle. Add sale listings separately through the manager inventory screens.

## Run locally

Install the .NET 10 SDK, then run these commands from the project folder.

```powershell
dotnet restore
dotnet run
```

Open the local URL printed in the terminal.

